[0.000, "o", "\r\n\r\nIntroduce a compiler error on purpose\r\n\r\n\u001b[38;2;92;112;104m│ The user wants me to introduce a compiler error on purpose. This is a bit unusual, but I'll do it. Let me first explor\u001b[39m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[38;2;92;112;104me the codebase to find a good place to introduce an error.\u001b[39m\r\n\r\nLet me first explore the codebase to find a good place to introduce an error:\r\n\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[38;2;167;192;128m✓\u001b[39m Find files\u001b[38;2;92;112;104m ('**/*.rs' (2 files))\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n\u001b[38;2;92;112;104m│ I found two Rust files. Let me read them to see what's in there, then I can introduce an intentional error.\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n\u001b[38;2;130;177;204m⠮\u001b[39m Read file\r\n\u001b[38;2;130;177;204m⠮\u001b[39m Read file\r\n\u001b[38;2;130;177;204m⣽\u001b[38;2;135;144;140m Tip: Type / to open the command picker\u001b[3m\u001b[38;2;92;112;104m  (esc to interrupt)\u001b[0m\u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\n\u001b[38;2;92;112;104m╭──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[38;2;92;112;104m│\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;212;221;214m> \u001b[39m                                                                                                                   \u001b[38;2;92;112;104m│\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b["]
