[0.053, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[2B\u001b[29A\r\u001b[J\u001b[38;2;92;112;104me the codebase to find a good place to introduce an error.\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n\r\u001b[JLet me first explore the codebase to find a good place to introduce an error:\r\n\r\n\u001b[38;2;167;192;128m✓\u001b[39m Find files\u001b[38;2;92;112;104m ('**/*.rs' (2 files))\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n\u001b[38;2;92;112;104m│ I found two Rust files. Let me read them to see what's in there, then I can introduce an intentional error.\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n\u001b[38;2;167;192;128m✓\u001b[39m Read file\u001b[38;2;92;112;104m (lib.rs, 95 lines)\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[38;2;167;192;128m✓\u001b[39m Read file\u001b[38;2;92;112;104m (error.rs, 50 lines)\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n\u001b[38;2;92;112;104m│ Now I'll introduce a simple compiler error. I'll introduce a type mismatch error in the `add` function by trying to re\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[38;2;92;112;104mturn a string instead of a u64.\u001b[39m\r\n\r\nI'll introduce a compiler error in the \u001b[38;2;143;188;176madd\u001b[39m function. Let me break it by returning the wrong type:\r\n\r\n\u001b[38;2;167;192;128m✓\u001b[39m Edit file\u001b[38;2;92;112;104m (lib.rs)\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[38;2;92;112;104m  31 \u001b[3m\u001b[38;2;92;110;"]
[0.000, "o", "101m/// ```\u001b[0m\u001b[39m\u001b[49m                                                \u001b[38;2;92;112;104m  31 \u001b[3m\u001b[38;2;92;110;101m/// ```\u001b[0m\u001b[39m\u001b[49m                                                \r\n\u001b[38;2;92;112;104m  32 \u001b[38;2;143;188;176m#[\u001b[38;2;212;221;214mmust_use\u001b[38;2;143;188;176m]\u001b[39m                                            \u001b[38;2;92;112;104m  32 \u001b[38;2;143;188;176m#[\u001b[38;2;212;221;214mmust_use\u001b[38;2;143;188;176m]\u001b[39m                                            \r\n"]
