[0.087, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[2B\u001b[29A\r\u001b[J\u001b[38;2;143;188;176mmismatched types\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[38;2;143;188;176mexpected `u64`, found `&str`\u001b[39m\r\n\r\u001b[J\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThe \u001b[38;2;143;188;176madd\u001b[39m function now tries to return a string literal (\u001b[38;2;143;188;176m\"this is a string, not a number\"\u001b[39m) instead of a \u001b[38;2;143;188;176mu64\u001b[39m, which causes \r\na type mismatch error. The function signature declares it returns \u001b[38;2;143;188;176mu64\u001b[39m, but the actual return value is \u001b[38;2;143;188;176m&str\u001b[39m.\r\n\r\nWould you like me to fix it, or introduce more errors? 😄\r\n\r\n\r\nNow fix the error,\r\n\r\n\u001b[38;2;92;112;104m│ The user wants me to fix the error I introduced. I'll change the add function back to the correct implementation.\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n\u001b[38;2;167;192;128m✓\u001b[39m Edit file\u001b[38;2;92;112;104m (lib.rs)\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[38;2;92;112;104m  31 \u001b[3m\u001b[38;2;92;110;101m/// ```\u001b[0m\u001b[39m\u001b[49m                                                \u001b[38;2;92;112;104m  31 \u001b[3m\u001b[38;2;92;110;101m/// ```\u001b[0m\u001b[39m\u001b[49m                                                \r\n"]
